{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-8",
  "title": "Self-Management as a discount",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Self-Management as a discount"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Below is a reflection on how the **concept** of offering a suggested SOW during onboarding, even for self-managed clients further enhances the **Design Joy–style subscription** for full-service product design and development:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Why It Works**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **Guidance Without Overreach**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Providing a **suggested SOW** (phases, approximate timelines, priority tips) acts as a guiding framework. The client still retains control over project management if they choose the self-managed tier."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **Reduced Risk of Mismanagement**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- A baseline plan mitigates the chance of clients prioritizing tasks poorly or misunderstanding time requirements. It’s a buffer against chaos, even when you’re not fully managing the project."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **Elevated Perceived Value**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- You show up as more than just “task executors.” Even for the cheaper, self-managed option, the client sees your **strategic insight** and feels cared for from the start."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. **Smooth Onboarding**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- By handing them a pre-structured approach, the client can start strong rather than fumbling through an empty queue. This clarity up front often prevents friction later."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "5. **Up-Sell Potential**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- When clients see how well thought-out your roadmap is, they might **upgrade** to the fully-managed tier to tap deeper into your project management and strategic expertise."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-16",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Potential Pitfalls**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-18",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-17",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Over-Dependence**"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- If you give them an SOW that’s too detailed, they may still want you to manage everything without paying for the higher tier. Keep it high-level enough that it’s valuable but not full-blown PM work."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-21",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-20",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**Misinterpretation**"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Some clients might treat the suggested SOW as a rigid guarantee of timeframes rather than a flexible guideline. Just clarify that it’s an **estimate**, subject to client decisions and real-world iteration."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-24",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Implementation Tips**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **SOW Format**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Phases**: Outline a typical flow (e.g., Discovery → Build → Feedback & Iteration → Launch)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **High-Level Milestones**: Provide rough durations: “Branding assets: 3–5 days,” “New features: 1–2 weeks each,” etc."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Priority Guidance**: Show which items should come first and how best to group or batch related tasks."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **Clear Disclaimer**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-30",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- Emphasize that this SOW is a starting point, not a set-in-stone project plan. Clients can modify it to fit their specific priorities."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-31",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **Communication Flow**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-32",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- For self-managed clients, have them confirm that they understand the SOW’s role and know how to allocate tasks in Linear (or whatever PM tool you use). If they get stuck, an upsell or an add-on project management service could be offered."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-33",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. **Onboarding Steps**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-34",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Sign Up** (client chooses self-managed or fully managed)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Receive SOW** (your baseline plan + disclaimers)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- **Orientation Call (Optional)**: A short session to walk them through the SOW and how to self-manage effectively."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-38",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Bottom Line**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-39",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Providing a **free, suggested SOW** during onboarding strikes a sweet spot: it reduces client missteps, showcases your expertise, and still keeps the door open for them to manage their own priorities. It’s a great way to **add tangible value** to the self-managed model without blurring the lines on what “fully managed” entails."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}